parate. Tradeoff:\n- Combined: fewer categories, simpler messages, but you lose the ability to say \"you typed 10k, likely meant 10\".\n- Separate: more precise, but more messages and more tests.\n\nGiven the course values consistent, tested behavior, and given they already have fine-grained categories in t3 (too_few/not_number/extra), I'd lean to **keep them distinct** for consistency: \"не число\" (no number at all) vs \"лишние символы после числа\" (partial parse). This mirrors t3's `not_number` vs `extra`. Actually t3's `extra` is \"too many coordinates\", not \"trailing junk\". Different. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what's most defensible and simplest:\n\nThe cleanest model for a *single argument with one number*:\n- No number at all → \"Радиус должен быть числом. Получено: X\"\n- Number, but extra content after (incl. inner space) → could reuse \"Радиус должен быть числом\" too, OR a distinct message.\n- Number out of range → distinct (already have).\n- inf/nan → distinct (already have).\n- <=0 → distinct (already have).\n- empty → distinct (already have via argc).\n\nHonestly, merging \"trailing junk\" into \"должен быть числом\" is the simplest and is what the code already does. The user's new message adds a category. Is it worth it? My recommendation: **it's optional; if you add it, do it because you can test it, and keep the name honest.** But be careful: adding a message that says \"лишние символы\" for `10 4` while `2 3` (two args) says \"лишние аргументы\" is a subtle but defensible distinction (content vs argc).\n\nActually, I think there's a stronger argument: **the user's proposal conflates two diagnostics that the user themselves cares about.** They earlier fought hard to distinguish `nan` (representable, just not valid here) from `1e400` (not representable), and \"too few\" vs \"too many\". Collapsing now would be a step *back* from the fine-grained model they built for t3. So I should challenge: is the added \"лишние символы\" category pulling its weight? If yes, define it as its own error code and test it. If not, keep the existing \"не число\" message (which already includes the received string, so the junk is visible).\n\nActually wait — re-reading the user: \"если в строке например \"10k\" или \"10 4\" то я не берусь разбирать точную ошибку, а кидаю что-то типа ...\". They're not necessarily adding a category; they're *simplifying* the diagnostic for the partial-parse case. They currently already have `radius_not_number` covering it, with message \"Радиус должен быть числом. Получено: 10k\". So their proposal is essentially a **message change**, not a category change. Good — that's simpler than I framed. So critique: changing the message to \"обнаружены лишние символы\" for ALL not-number cases would also apply to `abc` (where there are no \"extra symbols after a number\" — the whole thing is junk). So the message \"В полученной строке обнаружены лишние символы\" is misleading for `abc`: there's no base number. Unless they split categories.\n\nSo: if they keep ONE category, the message must be neutral for both `abc` and `10k`. \"Радиус должен быть числом. Получено: 10k\" is neutral and fine. If they want the \"лишние символы\" wording, they need a separate category for partial parse. This is the crux.\n\n**H. Another critical point: the generic message loses information the current one has.** Per § 4.6, message should say what was expected and what received. Both do. But the current per-category messages (finite/positive/range) are MORE specific and are exactly the kind of diagnostics the course wants. Their proposal for \"не берусь разбирать точную ошибку\" should be limited to the *junk* case, not extended to finite/positive/range — those are precisely identifiable and already tested. I should confirm they intend to keep those distinct. Likely yes.\n\n**I. Recommendation summary for Q2:**\n1. Keep the machine channel (exit 64 for all usage) — already done.\n2. Keep distinct categories that you can reliably detect and that carry information: not_number, not_finite, non_positive, out_of_range, empty. These map to different user mistakes.\n3. For the \"number + junk\" case: it's fine to either (a) fold into not_number, or (b) give a dedicated code+message \"лишние символы после числа\". Decide explicitly; if (b), it must not also swallow `abc` (no base number). Add tests for both.\n4. Don't let \"не берусь разбирать\" apply to finite/positive/range — those are exactly determinable and already tested.\n5. Empty: be explicit about \"no arg\" (argc<2) vs \"empty arg\" (argv[1]=\"\"), and note the harness currently can't pass an empty arg (unquoted `${args}` drops it). So today they're the same thing in tests. If you want to distinguish, that's a harness change.\n6. Consistency: apply the same token-error model to t3's coordinate parser so the two tasks don't diverge in wording for the same class.\n\n**J. Re Q1 more concretely.** Options on Windows:\n- `CreateProcessA/W` + correct quoting helper (current direction). Standard.\n- MSVC CRT `_spawnv`/`_execv` (`<process.h>`): takes argv array, CRT builds the command line with correct quoting. BUT: redirection must be done by manipulating the parent's std handles (`_dup2`) before spawn, which is racy/global and loses `CreateFile`/inheritance control. For a test runner needing three independent file redirections per child (and parallel ctest!), manipulating the parent's own std handles is unsafe. So not suitable. [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ for the API shape; МНЕНИЕ for \"not suitable\"]\n- `boost::process` / other libs: solve it, but that's a dependency (later layer).\n- Use `CommandLineToArgvW`'s inverse algorithm: implement a `quote_arg(std::string_view)` helper based on Microsoft Learn \"Parsing C++ command-line arguments\". Test it with a self-test (probe child).\n\nSo answer to Q1: **No, you cannot avoid the string on Windows** — the OS/`CreateProcess` boundary is a string. The fix is not elimination but a *correct, tested* serializer. On Linux you already have the pure vector via `execv`. Keep the `#ifdef` two-branch design; put the quoting in one small function with documented contract; cover it with a probe test. That converts the \"problem place\" from a silent risk into a tested component.\n\nAlso mention: the concatenation is inherent; what you *can* do is make the serialization correct and centralized. There's no API to pass argv vector to a Windows process (unlike POSIX). Even the native `NtCreateUserProcess` takes a `UNICODE_STRING CommandLine`. [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ for CreateProcess; СРЕДНИЙ for NtCreateUserProcess detail — mark to verify]\n\nLet me verify the NtCreateUserProcess claim: it takes RTL_USER_PROCESS_PARAMETERS which has CommandLine as UNICODE_STRING. Yes. High-ish. I'll mark СРЕДНИЙ.\n\n**K. One more nuance for Q1**: Even on POSIX, `execv` argv is separate, but if you ever used `system()` or a shell, you'd serialize. run_case uses execv, so fine. Good.\n\nNow, since this is plan mode, I should present analysis + a proposed plan, and ask clarifying questions. Let me structure the response:\n\n1. Q1 answer: no, unavoidable; options; recommendation (quote helper + probe test); note `_spawnv` alternative and why not.\n2. Q2 critique: \n   - what's good\n   - what's risky: the \"лишние символы\" message vs `abc`; don't collapse finite/positive/range; empty vs no-arg + harness limitation; consistency with t3.\n   - recommended model (table).\n3. Proposed plan (items), pending answers.\n4. Clarifying questions.\n\nKeep it reasonably concise but this is a design consultation. The user asked \"посмотри на мой подход критически - это вообще логично? дай совет, как сделать лучше\". So they want critique + advice. I can be thorough but structured.\n\nLet me also double check: does t4 C++ currently skip leading '+' AND handle spaces? Yes, trims then skips '+'. Good.\n\nNote on user proposal: \"если в строке после убирания пробелов по краям - одно число, то мы с ним работаем\". Must add: single finite, in-range, >0 number. Otherwise inf/1e400/negative slip. They have tests for those, so implementation likely keeps them; but phrasing the rule as \"одно число\" is incomplete. Flag.\n\nAlso: after trim, \"10 \" becomes \"10\" fine. \" 10 x \" → \"10 x\" inner junk.\n\nOne more: their empty message \"Ожидался радиус но он не был получен\" — grammar: \"Ожидался радиус, но он не был получен\" (comma). Minor style. And § 4.6 says no \"Ошибка:\" prefix — they're fine.\n\nLet me also mention: the categories should be an `enum class` in C++ and `enum`/constexpr in C, and ideally the *message mapping* in one place, so C and C++ can't drift. Currently t4 C and C++ duplicate the classification and messages; that's a drift risk (journal shows they've fought C/C++ divergence repeatedly). Suggest centralizing the categories (not necessarily the messages, due to printf/iostream) but at least keeping the enum values aligned. Actually since C and C++ share `common/`, could define `enum` in a shared header (C-compatible with `#ifdef __cplusplus` or just an enum). But messages differ by language; keep the *codes* shared. That's a good structural suggestion.\n\nNow the plan. Since plan mode, I'll outline a plan for when we implement. But the user may only want advice; I'll ask which they want.\n\nLet me write.\n\nFormat: headings, concise bullets. Mark [ФАКТ/МНЕНИЕ/ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ] and confidence.\n\nI should not be too long. But there's a lot. I'll aim for a focused but complete answer.\n\nLet me draft.\n\nFor Q1, key facts:\n- CreateProcessA/W: single string lpCommandLine. [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ]\n- No public Win32 API to pass argv vector. [ФАКТ, ВЫСОКИЙ]\n- CRT `_spawnv`/`_execv` take array, do quoting internally; but they don't offer STARTUPINFO redirection — you'd have to mutate the parent's handles. [ФАКТ про сигнатуру, МНЕНИЕ про непригодность]\n- Recommendation: keep CreateProcess + one `quote_arg()` helper implementing documented rules; add probe self-test.\n- On Linux: execv = true vector, nothing to do.\n\nFor Q2:\n- The plan needs a table of categories. Let me define:\n\n| Событие | Код (t4) | Сообщение |\n| argc<2 (нет аргумента) | usage | \"Ожидался радиус; значение не было передано\" |\n| argv[1] пустой после trim | usage | same as above |\n| нет числа вообще (abc, +abc) | usage | \"Радиус должен быть числом. Получено: X\" |\n| число + мусор (10k, 10 4, 0x10) | usage | либо тем же \"должен быть числом\", либо отдельное \"после числа следуют лишние символы: X\" |\n| inf/nan | usage | \"Радиус должен быть конечным числом. Получено: X\" |\n| <=0 | usage | \"Радиус должен быть положительным. Получено: X\" |\n| overlap/underflow | usage | \"Радиус выходит за пределы диапазона: X\" |\n\n- Critical: \"лишние символы\" wording is false for `abc`; so either separate the partial-parse case or use neutral wording.\n- Don't collapse finite/positive/range.\n- Empty vs no-arg: harness can't pass empty arg today.\n- t3 consistency.\n\nClarifying questions:\n1. Хочешь ли отдельную категорию \"число + мусор\" (с отдельным сообщением), или оставить объединённое \"должен быть числом\"?\n2. Различать ли \"аргумент отсутствует\" и \"аргумент — пустая строка\"? Если да — нужно править harness (сейчас невыразимо).\n3. Q1: делать ли self-test probe для run_case сейчас, или только корректный quote-хелпер?\n\nLet me write the final answer. Keep it structured, not overly long.\n\nActually, one more check for Q2: is there a difference between C and C++ currently in messages? Both use same Russian text (from mojibake, appear identical). Good.\n\nAlso note: t4 C++ `get_radius` returns `std::expected<double,int>` — good idiom. C uses out-param style. Fine.\n\nI'll mention centralizing codes in `common/` as an option.\n\nLet me write.",
