          "text": "The user asks two definitional questions:\n1. What does \"мой harness\" mean?\n2. What does \"контракт\" mean?\n\nI should explain both clearly, in the context of their project, with concrete references to their code. Keep concise but clear. Use analogies since they're in learning mode.\n\nHarness (обвязка/испытательный стенд) = the test infrastructure that surrounds the program under test: run_case, check, CMake test registration (add_case), ctest orchestration, fixtures, generators. It's not the product code (t1-t4 main), it's the code that runs the product, feeds input, captures output, compares, reports.\n\nAnalogy: испытательный стенд / прогонный стенд for an engine — the engine is the product (main.exe), the stand is the frame, sensors, fuel supply (harness). In Russian \"стенд\" or \"обвязка\". The term \"harness\" literally = упряжь/жгут проводов; in testing = test harness = тестовый стенд/обвязка.\n\nConcretely for them:\n- `tests/run_case.cpp` — launches the program, redirects streams, captures exit code.\n- `tests/check.cpp` — compares output files.\n- `tests/CMakeLists.txt` (`add_case`), `tests/cases.cmake` — describe cases, register with ctest.\n- `ctest` itself — runner.\n- input_data/expect — data (arguably fixtures).\n\n\"Мой harness\" in the sentence \"сначала довести свой harness\" = your own test stand: run_case + check + registration, as opposed to replacing it with boost::process.\n\nContract (контракт):\nTwo related meanings — I should distinguish:\n1. In programming generally: the set of guarantees a component makes about its behavior — preconditions, postconditions, invariants. Not the implementation, but the promise. Documented via comments (`@pre`/`@post`), types, tests.\n2. `[ФАКТ]` The AGENTS.md already uses this: § 4.3 \"контракты как документация (`@pre`/`@post` в Doxygen-комментариях)\".\n\nFor `quote_arg`: contract = \"given any string s, `quote_arg(s)` returns a command-line fragment such that when Windows parses it, the child receives exactly s as one argv element.\" Precondition: none (or s is valid). Postcondition: round-trip. The implementation (algorithm) is not the contract — the promise is. Tests verify the contract.\n\nAnalogy: контракт — как договор/техпаспорт: \"эта функция обязуется вернуть X при Y\", а код — как она это делает. Или как API-гарантия.\n\nAlso contract in CMake add_case: its contract = parameters meaning and what it registers.\n\nLet me give a concrete example of a contract in their code to make it tangible:\n- `parse_point` contract: pre — строка; post — `expected<Point,int>`, где error-коды означают ровно то-то; не читает stdin.\n- `run_case` contract: argv layout; post — запускает exe с ровно этими argv и редиректами, возвращает 0/1.\n\nI should keep it tight but useful. Maybe ask if they want me to draft the contract texts as part of the plan.\n\nPlan mode: no edits. Just explanation. Could offer to include contract drafts in the plan.\n\nLet me write concisely with structured sections and concrete references. Use Russian.\n\nAvoid over-long. Let me aim moderate.",
