poor fit for run_case specifically.\n\nLet me quickly verify some facts if possible. I can't run code, but I could webfetch Microsoft Learn docs for `_spawn`. That would strengthen accuracy. In plan mode, webfetch is read-only — allowed. Should I? It would help confirm exit-status semantics and inheritance. Let me consider: the user wants an answer, and accuracy matters (anti-sycophancy). Let me fetch the MSVC `_spawn` docs.\n\nLet me do a webfetch on https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-runtime-library/reference/spawnv-wspawnv and maybe _cwait.\n\nActually the relevant: `_spawn`, `_wspawn` Functions; and the `mode` constants. Let me fetch the spawn page.\n\nLet me do it — it's read-only and improves correctness.\n\nI'll fetch `_spawnv, _wspawnv`.\n\nLet me also fetch `_cwait` for status semantics.\n\nLet me run two webfetches in parallel.\n\nThen compose the answer.\n\nLet me do that.",
