radeoff; some editors/highlighters might still be confused.\n- Or use `[==[2\" 3]==]` — same bracket-type highlighting issue.\n\nI should be careful: is `\\\"` valid in CMake quoted arguments? Yes, CMake Escape Sequences include `\\\"`. So it works. But the project's convention/other bracket usages? They use `[=[...]=]` elsewhere maybe. Anyway, it's optional.\n\nSince plan mode, I only answer; no edits.\n\nLet me answer concisely: yes, UI artifact; CMake parsed it fine (proof: tests). Explanation: editor's highlighter mishandles `[=[...]=]` / the inner `\"`, treating the rest as string. Can ignore. If it bothers, `\"2\\\" 3\"` might highlight better, but not necessary.\n\nAlso note: the test passed, so no functional impact.\n\nI could offer to verify the exact value CMake stored by checking CTestTestfile? Not necessary. Actually I could mention that LastTest.log shows `\"2\\\" 3\"` serialized — but we already know tests pass.\n\nKeep it concise. The user asked a simple question.\n\nLet me write.",
